From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dianqk <dianqk@dianqk.net>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 10:24:55 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 25/29] board: mediatek-mobile: correct the A/B retry note of
 autoreset

LK decrements the retry counter of a slot that is not marked successful
on every boot, whatever the reset type; it does not ignore software
resets. The watchdog route stays: it also resets a hung U-Boot.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 board/mediatek/mediatek-mobile/mediatek-mobile.c | 9 +++++----
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/board/mediatek/mediatek-mobile/mediatek-mobile.c b/board/mediatek/mediatek-mobile/mediatek-mobile.c
index 498592165cb..634d1d4e76f 100644
--- a/board/mediatek/mediatek-mobile/mediatek-mobile.c
+++ b/board/mediatek/mediatek-mobile/mediatek-mobile.c
@@ -778,10 +778,11 @@ static bool mtk_usb_addressed(bool verbose)
 /*
  * Bring-up safety net: when "autoreset_s" is set (by the environment) and no
  * USB host has addressed the device within that many seconds, stop
- * servicing the watchdog. The stock bootloader counts the watchdog reset
- * (unlike a software reset) as a failed boot, so its A/B retry falls back
- * to the other slot; the console record is saved for the next boot. Once a
- * host connects, or "autoreset_s" is cleared, the device stays.
+ * servicing the watchdog. The watchdog also resets a U-Boot that hangs;
+ * the stock bootloader counts every boot of a slot not marked successful,
+ * so after a few attempts its A/B retry falls back to the other slot. The
+ * console record is saved for the next boot. Once a host connects, or
+ * "autoreset_s" is cleared, the device stays.
  */
 static struct cyclic_info mtk_autoreset;
 static ulong mtk_autoreset_start;
